      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If support was added everyone would buy one of these. It would move the immersion to the next level. But, if it’d be too much of a hassle to implement completely there could also be a soft implementation of the software. Unlike in Neos where it tracks every facial movement accurately, you could have it recognize a select few face patterns and bind them to the expressions on your avatar. Sort of like how it works with gestures but instead of clicking a button on your controller it just recognizes something basic like a smile or frown, and it shows on your avatar as a pre-made expression. Wouldn’t be as cool but definitely would be better than nothing.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
